Civil War was a massive crossover event pitting hero against hero over the issue of superhero registration.

The "Road to Civil War" which led up to this limited series ran through Amazing Spider-Man (Marvel, 1999 series) #529-531, Fantastic Four (Marvel, 1998 series) #536, 537 and the New Avengers: Illuminati (Marvel, 2006 series) #1 one-shot.

There was a Civil War: Opening Shot giveaway to promote the limited series and a number of one-shots and crossovers that tied in.

The Civil War crossover comics are as follows: 
[Limited Series]
- Civil War: Front Line (Marvel, 2006) #1-11;
- Civil War: X-Men (Marvel, 2006 series) #1-4;
- Civil War: Young Avengers & Runaways (Marvel, 2006 series) #1-4;
[Crossovers]
- Amazing Spider-Man (Marvel, 1999 series) #532-538;
- Black Panther (Marvel, 2005 series) #18, 23-25;
- Cable and Deadpool (Marvel, 2004 series) #30-32;
- Captain America (Marvel, 2004 series) #22-25;
